WEBVTT

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:04.270
The year is 2205 A.D.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:13.900
To annihilate the History Retrograde Army,
who scheme to alter history...

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.740
...we, who were born from swords...

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.290
...engage in mortal combat today as well!

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:29.040
<i>Meetings and partings (Yes! Yes!)</i>

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.210
<i>In the direction the sun rises (Yes! Yes!)</i>

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:42.730
<i>Now, let's move forward, one step at a time,</i>
<i>as each flower blossoms (Oh, yay!)</i>

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:47.770
"Touken Ranbu Hanamaru S2"

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:47.940
<i>(Woo!)</i>

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:55.530
<i>Rather than be anxious,</i>
<i>yes, it's better to believe</i>

00:00:55.530 --> 00:01:01.200
<i>Always rich in mind and spirit,</i>
<i>staying positive every day</i>

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:06.870
<i>Real strength is how we master what we each</i>

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:10.210
<i>Already have</i>

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:14.010
<i>If you try to rush virtue</i>

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:16.510
<i>It won't go well at all</i>

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:20.390
<i>Think as you look up at the sky</i>

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:25.730
<i>Step forward firmly, with assurance</i>

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:27.020
<i>Ready, set! Ready, go!</i>

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.020
<i>In a Hanamaru way</i>

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:31.650
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:34.990
<i>Without reserve</i>

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:39.570
<i>Under the bright, sunny sky</i>

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:42.120
<i>When you reach</i>

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:45.330
<i>The next street</i>

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:56.010
<i>Start walking again, one step at a time,</i>
<i>as each flower blossoms (Oh, woo!)</i>

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:03.260
A lot happened today, too, didn't it, Master?

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:06.600
Master, please rest well.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.690
"This anime is about the
stories of the Hanamaru days

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:15.730
of a certain group of
Sword Warriors in a certain citadel."

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:26.750
What did you just say?

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.870
Yes, I understand...

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:32.540
Excuse me.

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:38.510
Is something the matter?

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:46.140
Actually, it is possible that the
History Retrograde Army has appeared

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.060
in a new time period.

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:54.940
According to Master, it appears that
there is some unrest near the Edo period.

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:56.610
Should we tell everyone?

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:00.820
No, we still have too
little information right now.

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:04.120
It might just fuel their anxieties.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:05.740
That's true...

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:16.130
It's so cold...

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:18.170
Winter's almost here, isn't it?

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:22.010
The first winter since
our arrival at this citadel, huh?

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:26.720
On days like this, I bet it'd
be warm in General's bosom.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:29.140
What are you talking about all of a sudden?

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:33.020
Gotou, you wouldn't
want be in General's bosom?

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:36.230
I'm sure you'd feel all wrapped up.

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:39.740
I-I couldn't do something like that!

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.740
I want to be in it!

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:44.820
"Wives"
"Hot Springs with a
Married Woman Special Feature" "Fall Edition"

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:45.490
In a married woman's bosom!

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:50.370
And then have her pat
my head lots and spoil me.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:59.670
A-Anyway, we can't do something
so rude as to enter General's bosom.

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:01.720
Yeah, you're right...

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:05.760
If you're cold, why don't you
go to the dojo and move around?

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:07.390
Okay...

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:15.100
Excuse me.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:16.560
Shinano-<i>san</i>!

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:18.770
Do you want to spar with me?

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:22.240
Well, sparring's fine, too, but...

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:24.360
Hm?

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:25.780
I see.

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:29.990
So you're looking for a substitute
for Master's bosom, right?

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:33.040
How could he say something so extravagant...?

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:34.500
Huh? Did you say something?

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:36.880
N-No, nothing.

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:39.170
Then, it's easy!

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:42.300
I won't say it's the same as Master's...

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:46.510
...but I'll lend you my chest!

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:48.390
Huh?!

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:58.690
Bosom...

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:03.690
But...

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:07.030
How is it?

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:10.080
I... I can't breathe!

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:12.620
That looks fun!

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:15.210
Please let me join you!

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:18.750
M-My... breath...

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:20.500
Will they be okay?

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:26.880
I wonder if there's anything
that can substitute for a bosom?

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:27.930
Welcome back!

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:30.140
You worked hard, didn't you?

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:32.850
Your training was hard, wasn't it?

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:35.480
Yeah, but I've become stronger!

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:38.190
Aizen, you're back? Welcome home.

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:40.560
Yup, I'm back!

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:43.230
Are you okay?

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:47.610
Actually, I've been roaming
the citadel looking for warmth...

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:49.660
Warmth, huh?

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:50.910
In that case...

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:54.290
Excuse me.

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:58.170
Nikkari-<i>san</i>, can I join you in the <i>kotatsu</i>?

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:01.000
Oh, Shinano-<i>kun</i>. I don't mind.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:03.170
All right, thanks!

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:09.760
If I go in up to my shoulders,
it feels like I'm all wrapped up.

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:11.350
That's true.

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:15.180
It's warm and soft, a little like a bosom.

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:16.640
That's true.

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:26.070
Nikkari-<i>san</i>, wanna talk about something?

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:27.280
Sure.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:30.490
Anything interesting happen to you lately?

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:32.620
Interesting, huh...?

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:37.120
Now that you mention it, the other day...

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:42.790
I returned from a dispatch at night...

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:44.920
Oh?

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:11.570
You can stop telling that story now!

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:12.320
Are you sure?

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:14.030
It was plenty interesting already!

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:16.120
Thanks!

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:22.290
Well, it was just Oodenta-<i>san</i> leaving the bath.

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:29.130
That was scary...

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:40.600
Even simple tasks are pleasurable when I think
of how Master will savor and delight in this.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.730
Food is important.

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:46.980
As the saying goes, "You can't worry
about etiquette on an empty stomach."

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:51.360
Besides...

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:58.410
...if we master this work, we may be able
to open up a new path to enlightenment.

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:02.460
So, were you able to open up a new path?

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:05.630
It's different from a bosom somehow...

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:07.960
Oh, it was no good?

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:12.720
It's smooth and glossy and soft...

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:15.840
...but there's not enough of a squeeze.

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:19.560
It's too bad I was unable to help.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:25.230
This isn't quite right...

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:26.650
This isn't right...

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:27.940
Nue!

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:32.860
This isn't right, either.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:37.490
There's something that isn't
quite right about all of them...

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:43.370
Do you long for a bosom that badly?

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:48.460
Then I will bare all to help you out.

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:49.460
Huh?

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:53.630
I've heard that humans will undress
to warm each other when it's cold.

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:55.260
Huh?

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:57.760
Come, let us warm each other!

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:00.180
N-No thanks!

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:03.680
Wait a minute!

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:07.560
You don't have to be shy.

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:11.360
I'm not being shy,
and I've had enough of muscles!

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:17.820
Shinano-<i>kun</i>, where did you go?

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:19.950
Let's make each other nice and warm!

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:23.910
He's gone.

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:29.790
Hey, he's gone, so come out.

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:34.550
This place is pretty good...

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:35.300
Wha--?!

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:41.390
You're warm, and the cloth is
a little dirty, but wraps around me,

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:44.390
and it smells good, too.

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:47.390
That's enough! Hurry up and get out!

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:50.730
Just a little longer!

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:54.740
--Let. Go. Of. Me!
--Please...!

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:58.740
Too bad... That was pretty close...

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:06.710
I guess even if I'll get scolded,
I have no choice but to ask the general.

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:09.580
General!

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:13.840
Shinano, perfect timing!

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:19.510
Can you help me carry this?

00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:25.890
They're clothes Master made
for us to protect against the cold.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:32.310
--Master spent many months working
steadily on these to prepare them for us.
--So cute!

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:34.860
This will keep me warm.

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:40.200
I'll wear this when
I sit on the porch drinking tea.

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:45.580
All right! I'll wear this tomorrow
and go to the general store!

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:52.710
Master! I will treasure
this scarf for the rest of my life!

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:56.300
Master!

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:59.510
Shinano, what did you get?

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:02.590
I feel like I'm wrapped in someone's bosom!

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:04.220
It's so warm.

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:17.820
It's about time you came back.

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:38.960
"Date Residence"

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:48.890
Gather round!

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:54.270
The History Retrograde Army
has appeared in a new time period.

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:58.110
You all know how strong
the enemy was at the Ikeda Inn.

00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:02.320
It's highly possible that they
will be even stronger than that.

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:05.740
They have appeared in 1747 in the Edo period.

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:11.330
And we believe the enemy is after
Date Munemura and Hosokawa Munetaka.

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:15.790
You don't mean <i>that</i> incident?

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:20.550
If I remember correctly, Lord Munetaka
was killed inside Edo Castle, right?

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:22.010
Yes.

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:23.970
Because he did not yet have a successor,

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:28.560
if Munetaka died, the Hosokawa family
would have been crushed.

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:32.430
The sixth daimyo of the Date family,
Munemura, happened to pass by

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:36.940
and, thinking quickly, he lied, saying,
"Lord Munetaka is still alive,"

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:40.480
saving the Hosokawa family
from their predicament.

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:45.410
In other words, they want to kill
Lord Date Munemura before that incident

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:47.870
and bring about the downfall
of the Hosokawa family?

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:50.040
We won't let them!

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:54.920
We will send you to the day
before the incident, August 14th.

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:59.090
Protect Date Munemura
and stop the enemy's schemes!

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:02.460
"Sa"

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:03.170
I will now announce who
will be dispatched for this mission.

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:05.340
Tantou, Sayo Samonji.

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:06.890
Very well.

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:09.350
Tantou, Taikogane Sadamune.

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:10.850
I'm itching to use my skills!

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:13.390
Uchigatana, Kasen Kanesada.

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:19.860
I will not allow any alterations
to the history of the Hosokawa family.

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:22.530
Tachi, Shokudaikiri Mitsutada.

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:25.240
I will definitely accomplish my mission.

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:27.740
Tachi, Tsurumaru Kuninaga.

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:28.950
Leave it to me.

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:30.910
"Sa"

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:30.530
And the captain will be...

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:35.330
...uchigatana, Ookurikara.

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:43.670
Kara-<i>bou</i>'s the captain?

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:47.590
I heard that you are a sword
passed down in the Date family,

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:50.600
so I believe you also know Lord Munemura.

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:54.270
We're counting on you!

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:57.310
Then, you will be dispatched in thirty minutes.

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:10.070
I have close ties to the Hosokawa family.

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:15.910
I was impatient, and ended up coming early.

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:21.040
Since someone from the Date family that
treasured you for so long was being targeted,

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:23.710
you couldn't relax either, could you?

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:27.010
For this mission, you are the captain.

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:29.220
I'm counting on you.

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:31.050
I have no intention of flocking together.

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:35.640
Sorry, were you waiting long?

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:38.100
No, it's fine.

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:42.020
Besides, there is still a lot of time
before we were told to meet.

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:45.030
I wanted to be dispatched
as soon as possible and couldn't wait.

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:47.740
It appears we all felt the same way.

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:49.660
Everyone's here?

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:54.410
Ookurikara.

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:57.620
"Sword Protection"

00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:00.710
This is from Master.

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:02.920
We don't know what
strong enemies will await you.

00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:04.290
Take this with you.

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:06.210
All right.

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:09.720
Of course, it is our duty
to prevent alterations to history.

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:16.220
But it will not be considered
successful unless you all return safely.

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:18.520
Captain Ookurikara,

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:24.610
the captain's most important mission is to
make sure everyone returns without breaking.

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:27.280
Don't be mistaken in your judgment.

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:33.450
Munemura should be in the
Date family's samurai residence

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:35.580
in the Sendai Domain of the Edo castle town.

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:37.040
Very well.

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:38.330
Let's go.

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:50.050
According to what Konnosuke said,

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:54.180
Lord Munemura should not be going anywhere.

00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:58.140
I've confirmed it.

00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:01.140
Lord Munemura is inside the residence.

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:05.980
Sayo went to tell Kasen and Tsuru-<i>san</i>,
who are waiting in the back.

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:10.030
If they are going to act, it would be
tonight or tomorrow morning, huh?

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:12.360
I think they'd be more likely to act tonight

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:15.780
than in the morning
when they're more likely to be seen.

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:19.120
I don't want to get humans
involved if we can help it.

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:22.960
"I would like to talk privately.

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:27.090
Come to the castle today at sundown," huh?

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:31.800
Elder Hotta Masasuke has called for us.

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:32.970
Prepare to depart!

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:34.550
Yes, sir!

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:46.400
Munemura has come out of the residence.

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:51.490
Where could he be going at this hour?

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:53.700
We're following him.

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:59.580
It looks like he's heading to Edo Castle.

00:17:17.590 --> 00:17:18.800
They've appeared, huh?

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:22.060
It was the History Retrograde Army's
doing after all, huh?

00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:24.730
Hurry up and scatter!

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:31.400
Sada!

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:33.190
Osayo!

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:34.490
There.

00:17:37.070 --> 00:17:38.280
Die already.

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:43.830
You're too slow!

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:45.790
Let's go, let's go, let's go!

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:51.960
Take this!

00:17:57.720 --> 00:17:59.050
Die.

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:04.520
You're so obvious.

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:11.610
I won't let you!

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:20.030
It doesn't matter how much you defend!

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:26.040
As expected of Micchan!

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:28.000
I'm going, too!

00:18:33.050 --> 00:18:34.960
Excellent!

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:36.760
I want to look cool...

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:40.050
...finishing them off, too!

00:18:47.940 --> 00:18:50.520
I did it... I think?

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:03.740
Behind you.

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:09.710
Is that all of them?

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:11.380
No.

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:13.670
Doesn't look like they'll let us pass yet.

00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:32.560
You're the only one left, huh?

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:53.630
I'll have your head!

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:06.810
Carelessness is our greatest enemy.

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:14.150
That took longer than I expected, though.

00:20:14.150 --> 00:20:15.900
Let's hurry up and follow them!

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:22.030
This is bad. The sun's about to set.

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:27.910
No one's here?

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:33.790
Wh-Who's there?!

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:39.590
My lord! Please, stay back!

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:46.050
Why did the History Retrograde Army
not kill Lord Munemura at the residence

00:20:46.050 --> 00:20:48.060
but go out of their way
to call him out to Edo Castle?

00:20:48.060 --> 00:20:50.060
They could be planning to destroy
not just the Hosokawa family,

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:52.310
but the Date family, as well.

00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:53.690
What did you say?

00:20:53.690 --> 00:20:58.400
If Lord Munemura dies in the
middle of the night inside Edo Castle,

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:02.740
then they could easily make it seem
like he snuck in plotting something

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:04.320
and was killed when they tried to stop him.

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:07.740
It appears the enemy also
used their brains a little, huh?

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:09.660
Enough with the idle chatter.

00:21:17.840 --> 00:21:19.460
Oh no, you don't!

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:22.460
I won't let you lay a finger on them!

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:39.360
We haven't seen these guys before.

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:41.570
Let's take care of them quickly.

00:21:54.710 --> 00:21:56.170
It's raining...

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:04.630
Oh, no! Ookurikara
and the others are in trouble!

00:23:55.030 --> 00:24:01.590
"More <i>Hanamaru</i> Next Week!!"
